tandem (4.53) unstable; urgency=medium

  * The A3 fiscal certificate: name the missing service, not a four-step recipe.
    A Brazilian counter cannot legally emit an invoice without its A3
    certificate token (a smartcard) working, and when a Windows program imports
    winscard.dll Tandem recognised the case and printed a fixed four-line
    procedure - install pcscd, pcsc-tools, libccid, run pcsc-scan. But it never
    looked at the machine first, and docs/IDEAS.md had already measured that the
    single most common cause is the simplest one: the smartcard service is not
    installed at all. So a shop whose only problem was a missing pcscd read a
    wall of steps instead of the one that mattered. Now, exactly as it already
    does for the Sentinel and CodeMeter hardware keys, Tandem checks the machine
    before it speaks: if the pcsc software is absent it says so - "the smartcard
    service is not installed; that is almost always the whole problem" - and if
    it is installed but the daemon is not running it says that instead. Both
    facts are read without privilege and before any download. The static verdict
    still carries the honest ceiling (a reader Linux can see is not yet a
    certificate that will sign), so nothing is over-promised.
    - The decision reuses the key-status shape (`t_chave_estado pcsc` reports
      INSTALADO and SERVICO; `t_texto_chave pcsc` turns them into the sentence),
      so the smartcard path sits beside sentinel/codemeter rather than being a
      special case, and is proven by injection: a machine without pcscd gets the
      "not installed" line, one with the daemon down gets "not running", and one
      with it up gets nothing extra.
    - Two new messages, `pcsc_falta` and `pcsc_parado`, translated in all seven
      languages.

