tandem (4.51) unstable; urgency=medium

  * python3 is now a piece `tandem preparar` ensures, which matters only off
    Debian. The six file readers (peinfo, apkinfo, appimageinfo, jarinfo,
    debinfo, rpminfo) are Python, so without python3 Tandem cannot read an
    .exe, .apk, .AppImage, .jar or foreign .rpm at all - the whole diagnosis
    layer goes dark. On apt that never bites: python3 is a hard dependency of
    the .deb. But the generic bundle does no dependency resolution, and
    dnf5-based Fedora and Arch base ship NO python3 - so a shop owner who
    installed Tandem there had a reader layer that could not run. preparar now
    installs it: `t_pecas_faltando` lists python3 when it is missing, and
    `t_pacote_familia` maps it to the family's package (python3 on dnf/zypper,
    `python` on Arch - which still provides /usr/bin/python3, verified on a real
    Arch). Confirmed on real Fedora 41 and Arch: preparar installs python3, and
    a reader that could not run before runs afterwards.
  * The apt install plan gains a python3 case too, as belt-and-braces for a
    Debian machine where it somehow went missing; on apt it is normally already
    there. One new piece message (peca_python3), translated in all seven
    languages. No behaviour change on apt.

