tandem (4.39) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Harden the two guards the vision audit surfaced last; both are test-only,
    with no change to what the program does.
  * A `.msi` is opened with `wine msiexec /i`, never `wine file.msi` (which
    always fails because a `.msi` is not a PE). `executar()` has always routed
    it there, but nothing guarded that a later refactor keeps doing so - a
    "simplification" to `wine "$PROG"` would make every `.msi` fail and send the
    dependency loop hunting for DLLs that are not the problem. A full-loop test
    now runs a `.msi` through a fake wine and asserts the `msiexec /i`
    invocation, and that the file is never handed straight to wine; proven both
    ways by injection.
  * The no-function-defined-twice guard knew only the `name()` spelling, so a
    duplicate written `name ()` or `function name` could walk around it. The
    extractor now folds all three spellings to the bare name, stays anchored at
    column 0 so awk's own indented `function`s are left alone, and requires
    parentheses or the keyword so an assignment is never mistaken for a
    definition. Each spelling has its own vacuity probe.

