tandem (4.25) unstable; urgency=medium

  * `tandem portas fixar COM3 /dev/ttyUSB0` REPORTED SUCCESS AND OPENED
    NOTHING. It wrote only the registry key HKLM\Software\Wine\Ports and
    stopped, but what makes a port openable is the dosdevices/comN symlink Wine
    mints for a port it auto-detected. Measured with real Wine and a real char
    device: with only the registry key, a program calling CreateFile("COM3") -
    which is exactly what ACBr's PosPrinter does - gets "File not found", byte
    for byte identical to a port that was never set. So the one command
    CLAUDE.md documents as the printer and pinpad remedy said "done" while the
    device stayed unreachable - the silent failure this project exists to end.
  * fixar now creates the symlink first and writes the registry key second,
    best-effort. The symlink is the half that OPENS the port; the registry key
    is the OTHER half, populating SERIALCOMM so the port APPEARS in a program's
    dropdown. A failed registry write no longer fails the command, because
    opening is the point and enumeration is only the nicety.
  * soltar now removes both halves, and only ever removes a symlink IT could
    have made - a plain file someone mounted at dosdevices/comN by hand is left
    untouched, and the port name is validated before any path is deleted.
  * Proven by injection: with the symlink line removed the command still says
    "done" and no dosdevices/comN appears, so the new test fails exactly where
    the old code was silent.

