tandem (4.22) unstable; urgency=medium

  * THE SETTINGS FILE COULD END UP WITH THE SAME KEY TWICE, holding two
    different values. It is a read-modify-write on one file every command
    touches, and the temp file it went through was named
    "$TANDEM_CONFIG.novo" - FIXED, not per process - so two writers at once
    truncated the same name and interleaved into it. Measured with four
    concurrent writers of sixty keys each: CHAVE_A and CHAVE_C both came out
    present twice. t_config_le takes `tail -1`, so the reader then picks
    whichever duplicate landed last, which in that run was the OLDER value.
  * Not a corner. t_lista_talvez_atualiza stamps LISTA_DIA from a DETACHED
    background process that tandem-exe spawns on its way to opening a program,
    so an ordinary double click already has two writers.
  * What lives in that file is why this is worse than untidy. ENVIO_HOJE and
    ENVIO_ESPERA_ATE are the caps that stop a machine with no route to the
    address retrying every queued line all day. And RECEBER and ENVIAR are the
    owner's own on/off choice for the community list - a duplicate read from
    the wrong line can turn back on something he turned off, which is consent
    rather than a setting.
  * Fixed with a per-process temp name AND a lock: the name alone stops the
    interleaving, but two complete writes would still race on the move and one
    key would simply vanish. The lock is best-effort by the rule the prefix
    lock already follows - a lock that cannot be CREATED, on a full disk or a
    read-only home, must never be mistaken for a lock that is taken.
  * Two sweeps held with nothing to fix and are recorded because they cost the
    same time: the community list's signature path answers correctly on all
    five branches, exercised with real Ed25519 keys - a file signed by ANOTHER
    key is refused, an unreadable signature is refused, and an absent one is
    accepted, which is the documented transition policy. And the file
    disappearing from under all nine handlers the instant they start - a pen
    drive unplugged - produces a sentence naming the path in every one of
    them, with no silence, no bash error and no traceback.

