tandem (4.21) unstable; urgency=medium

  * The panel a shop owner who never opens a terminal sees was eighteen rows of
    equally weighted grey prose, of which eight fitted the window, with nothing
    saying the other ten existed. It is two screens now - the things a shop
    does, then one row that opens the rest - and it still carries ALL EIGHTEEN
    commands. Shortening it by dropping commands would take function away from
    the one person who cannot get it back from a terminal.
  * Every row has an icon. zenity --imagelist takes a PATH and draws a broken
    placeholder for an icon NAME - measured side by side in one window - so the
    name is resolved to a path at runtime, and a machine where nothing resolves
    gets the plain list it has today rather than a row of broken squares.
  * An optional dark look, off by default. `tandem tema escuro` turns it on and
    `tandem tema sistema` puts it back; with no choice made nothing changes at
    all. A shop machine set up in the light running a Tandem that forces itself
    dark is worse than plain - it looks broken - so this is asked for, never
    assumed, the same way the language is.
  * It applies to Tandem's own windows and nothing else on the machine, through
    GTK_THEME, which is per process. Three attempts failed in silence first and
    each looked like "it cannot be done": zenity here is 4.0.1 and links GTK4,
    so a gtk-3.0/ theme is ignored without a word. `GTK_THEME=Adwaita:dark` is
    the one-command test that separated "cannot" from "wrong folder". Both GTK
    versions ship.
  * The theme lives under /usr/share/tandem rather than /usr/share/themes:
    measured, a theme in a private directory loads through XDG_DATA_DIRS, and
    one installed system-wide would appear in the owner's theme picker as
    something he never asked for.
  * Stated because a limit hidden is a limit that surprises somebody later: the
    window, the sunken tray, the buttons, the entry, the scrollbar and the
    progress bar are CSS boxes and take the whole treatment. The rows inside
    zenity's list draw their selected state on a node no selector reached -
