tandem (4.18) unstable; urgency=medium

  * The six readers now defend their own KEY=VALUE contract instead of relying
    on the input format to defend it for them. Everything they print is either
    a number they computed or a STRING THAT CAME OUT OF THE FILE, and the file
    arrived from the internet on a machine belonging to somebody who is not a
    programmer. Whether such a string can carry a newline is a property of the
    SOURCE format: a .deb control file is line-based and cannot, while a PE
    import name, an RPM header string and an Android manifest string are
    length- or NUL-delimited and carry one perfectly well. Thirty-five print
    sites, all of them cleaned on the way out.
  * The asymmetry that made it visible, and the argument that it was an
    oversight rather than a decision: peinfo's raw-exception path already did
    .replace("\n", " ") while the data path three lines below it did not.
    Somebody thought about the problem and covered half of it.
  * This is defence in depth, not a live failure - no real .exe has a newline
    in a DLL name. It is asserted anyway, in both directions: the six cannot be
    made to forge a line, AND an ordinary value comes through untouched. The
    second assertion is not decoration; without it a cleaner that erased
    everything would pass the first.
  * Found by tests/fuzz-leitores.py, new here: it corrupts VALID files and
    insists the readers answer rather than crash, hang, eat the machine or
    print half a line. Random bytes are the easy case - every reader already
    dies on the magic number and says so. What breaks a parser is a file that
    gets past the magic and then lies.
  * The fuzzer had two defects of its own, both fixed and both written into its
    header. It ran THREE mutations while reporting "every one answered",
    because a bare-number argument swallowed the seed's value; and it INVENTED
    a finding using Python's splitlines(), which breaks on form feed where the
    shell does not. A tool that invents findings is worse than one that misses
    them.

